{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "speaking/a-hook-can-silence-the-decision-taken-after-thinking-non-streaming",
  "title": "A hook can silence the decision taken after thinking (non-streaming)",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4",
    "§9.2"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-9.2-064"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: tests/test_speak_decision_hooks.py::test_the_decision_taken_again_once_the_agent_thought_goes_through_the_hooks. Real policy, thinker, hooks and model boundaries are observed separately; gates make late return explicit, without wall-clock duration assertions. The two changes during one answering turn retain exact previous/new pairs without imposing an order on async observers.",
  "setup": {
    "channels": [
      {
        "id": "ws",
        "type": "websocket",
        "category": "transport"
